{"BlockedEmail.should_block? performs database writes (updating match_count and last_match_at) during validation, violating the principle that validation should be read-only and creating unnecessary write load": 0.7122842073440552, "Email lookup does not perform canonicalization (downcase, strip), meaning 'User@Example.com' and 'user@example.com' would be treated as different emails, potentially bypassing blocks": 0.8180818557739258, "rejectedEmails array grows unbounded and may accumulate duplicate entries if user retries with same email multiple times - should check if email exists before adding": 0.300368070602417, "rejectedEmails array should be reset when modal is closed or successful submission occurs to prevent stale client-side state": 0.19376923143863678, "BlockedEmail stats are not captured for emails already blocked by domain whitelist/blacklist policies, which may result in incomplete telemetry": 0.25122714042663574}